<node id="1232647" title="Re: Getting for() to accept a tied array in one statement" created="2019-04-16 08:15:57" updated="2019-04-16 08:15:57" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="1021810">hdb</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;
Never used &lt;c&gt;tie&lt;/c&gt; before, so this is a good learning experience, even though like [LanX] I do not know either what this is good for. In any case, I think, this works as required:
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;code&gt;
for( @{ tie my @x, "My::Class", "first", "second"; \@x } ) {
	print "$_\n";
}
&lt;/code&gt;</doctext>
